WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.752
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:06.400
SPEAKER: Today I'm
going to show you

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.790
how to get started using EDB
Postgres Enterprise Database

00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:11.510
in Google Cloud Launcher.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:15.090
EDB Postgres Enterprise provides
comprehensive management,

00:00:15.090 --> 00:00:17.940
integration, and Oracle
compatibility and migration

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:22.740
tools, as well as services
and 24/7 global support.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.540
From the EDB Postgres
Enterprise landing

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:30.590
page on the Cloud Launcher site,
click Launch on Compute Engine.

00:00:30.590 --> 00:00:33.420
This will take you to the Select
or Create a Project, where

00:00:33.420 --> 00:00:36.360
you can make your selection.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.830
Next, you'll be taken to
the Deployment Configuration

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:41.580
page, where you can
customize your instance

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:46.470
and choose a name, a zone,
a machine type, a boot disk

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:49.780
image, network access,
and additional options

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:52.460
like management, disk
networking, access,

00:00:52.460 --> 00:00:54.050
and security options.

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:56.100
The defaults are
designed to work well,

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:01.220
so we'll simply select Deploy,
and you're ready to go.

00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:03.430
To get started with
EDB Postgres Enterprise

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:06.530
on Cloud Launcher, click on
the link in the comments.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:08.340
Thanks for watching.

